Package: meizu-e3-dkms
Version: 0.1.7
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Meizu E3 Port <maintainer@localhost>
Installed-Size: 799
Depends: dkms (>= 2.1.0.0), xinput, x11-xserver-utils
Recommends: device-tree-compiler
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/
Description: Meizu E3 display and touch integration (DKMS)
 Driver and device-tree overlay sources live under /usr/src/meizu-e3-dkms-<ver>/
 (Makefile, drivers/, overlay/). DKMS builds kernel modules on the target at
 configure time; postinst compiles the overlay to /boot/dtbo/*.dtbo.disabled
 when dtc is available.
 The desktop autostart helper maps the touchscreen to DSI-1 and reapplies the
 mapping after display layout changes.
 .
 This package does not depend on Debian/Ubuntu archive kernel headers: install
 linux-headers matching your running kernel (uname -r) from your vendor or
 board image repository (e.g. Radxa) before expecting DKMS or overlay build to
 succeed.
